ith the established procedures, with due regard for the rights of the persons featured in the content.", "Members may report abusive content or content that violates the rules of use through the reporting tools provided in the app. The administration will review reports and take appropriate action within no more than twenty-four (24) hours, including removing the offending content and, where necessary, restricting the permissions of, or blocking access by, the offending user.", "Every member may block any other user from within the app, which prevents that user's content from appearing to them and prevents that user from contacting them. The app administration is notified of blocks so that it can review the relevant content where necessary."], "summary": "Posts are reviewed before publishing; you can report and block, and every report is reviewed within 24 hours."}, {"id": "tree", "title": "Management of the Family Tree and Lineage Data", "lines": ["The Al-Mohammad Ali Family app aims to document the family tree and preserve family ties by displaying information drawn from family sources, genealogical charts, historical documents, and approved data.", "Approved members may submit requests to add their children and other individuals connected to them by a recognised family relationship within the family tree, in accordance with the permissions and rules set out in the app. Adding any other person requires a special request to the app administration for consideration.", "Requests to add individuals or to amend or correct their data are subject to review and verification by the app administration before they are approved and the changes appear in the family tree.", "Users must take care to ensure the accuracy and correctness of information about lineage and family relationships, and must not knowingly provide misleading or undocumented data.", "The app administration may request the supporting information or documents needed to verify requests, with due regard for the privacy of data subjects and without collecting more information than is necessary for verification.", "The display of information in the family tree does not constitute official proof of lineage and is not a substitute for documents and records issued by the competent authorities.", "Data subjects or their legal representatives may submit requests to correct, update, hide, or delete their information. Such requests are handled in accordance with the Privacy Policy, the established rules, and applicable regulations."], "summary": "Adding or editing in the tree is by request reviewed by the admins; the tree is not official proof of lineage."}, {"id": "admin", "title": "Administrative and Moderation Powers", "lines": ["The Al-Mohammad Ali Family app administration oversees the operation of the app, organises its services, and manages memberships, permissions, and family content in a manner that serves the app's objectives and safeguards the integrity of information and the privacy of members.", "Administrative and moderation permissions are granted to persons authorised by the app administration according to their duties and responsibilities, and they may not use these permissions beyond the authorised purposes.", "The app administration and its moderators, each within the limits of their permissions, may review requests for membership, additions, and amendments, examine content and reports, and take appropriate action to address violations in accordance with the rules of use.", "The administration may modify or restrict members' permissions, or suspend or terminate membership, where there are legitimate reasons to do so, ensuring that the action taken is proportionate to the nature and severity of the violation.", "Administrators and moderators must keep confidential the data they access in the course of their duties and must not disclose it or use it for personal gain or for unauthorised purposes.", "Users may appeal administrative decisions concerning their membership, permissions, or content. The app administration will review and respond to the appeal within no more than seven (7) calendar days from the date it is received, and will inform the user of the outcome through the means of communication available in the app."], "summary": "Admins have limited, task-based permissions, and you can appeal their decisions within 7 days."}, {"id": "suspension", "title": "Suspension and Termination of Membership", "lines": ["The Al-Mohammad Ali Family app administration may temporarily suspend or terminate a user's membership if the user violates the rules of use, provides misleading information, misuses the app's services or the permissions granted to them, or engages in any conduct that may harm the security of the app or the privacy of its members.", "In taking such action, the nature, severity, and recurrence of the violation are taken into account. The administration may take immediate measures where there is an actual risk to the security of the app or the integrity of members' data, without prejudice to the user's right of appeal.", "The administration determines the length of a temporary suspension according to the nature and severity of the violation and reviews whether continued suspension is necessary. A suspension may be extended only for a justified reason, and the user will be informed accordingly.", "The user will be informed of the reason for the suspension or termination of their membership and of the action taken against them through the available means of communication, unless a legitimate legal or security reason prevents this.", "Users may appeal a decision to suspend or terminate their membership. The app administration will review and respond to the appeal within seven (7) calendar days from the date it is received, in accordance with the established procedures.", "Suspension or termination of membership does not constitute automatic deletion of the account or the personal data associated with it, and the user retains the right to request deletion of their account in accordance with Section 9 of the Privacy Policy.", "Termination of membership does not necessarily result in the deletion of lineage data from the family tree; only the name and family relationship may be retained, where permitted under the Privacy Policy and applicable regulations."], "summary": "Membership may be suspended for violations, with the reason given, and you can appeal."}, {"id": "ip", "title": "Intellectual Property Rights", "lines": ["The intellectual property rights in the name, logo, design, interfaces, software, and databases of the Al-Mohammad Ali Family app belong, to the extent permitted by law, to the owner of the app or to the rights holders who have licensed the use of their works.", "The app may not be copied, and no protected component of it may be reproduced, modified, distributed, or exploited for commercial purposes, without the prior consent of the rights holder.", "Users retain their lawful rights in the original photos, text, and other content they submit through the app, and publishing such content does not transfer its ownership to the app administration.", "Users grant the app administration a non-exclusive licence, limited to legitimate family purposes, to store, display, and process the content they submit to the extent necessary to operate the app's services and provide them to approved members, subject to the Privacy Policy and the rights of data subjects.", "Names, historical facts, and genealogical information are not, in themselves, the exclusive intellectual property of the app, without prejudice to any rights that may subsist in legally protected works, photos, or databases.", "Users must not post any content that infringes the intellectual property rights of others. Rights holders may submit reports to the app administration requesting the review or removal of infringing content."], "summary": "What you post stays yours; copying the app or its components is not allowed."}, {"id": "updates", "title": "Amendments to the Rules of Use", "lines": ["The Al-Mohammad Ali Family app administration reserves the right to amend or update these Terms and Rules of Use when necessary, in line with the development of the app's services, regulatory and legal requirements, or the measures needed to protect members and their data.", "The app administration will publish the updated version of the rules of use within the app, stating the date of the last update, and will notify members of material changes at least fourteen (14) calendar days before they take effect.", "The advance notice period does not apply to changes required to address urgent security risks or to comply with legal obligations that require immediate application; users will be informed of such changes as soon as possible.", "Where changes require the user's fresh consent under applicable regulations, the user's continued use of the app will not alone be treated as consent to those changes.", "Changes will not apply retroactively in a way that diminishes the rights users have under applicable laws and regulations.", "Users who do not wish to continue under the updated rules may stop using the app and request deletion of their account in accordance with the Privacy Policy."], "summary": "We notify you of material changes 14 days before they take effect."}, {"id": "law", "title": "Governing Law and Dispute Resolution", "lines": ["These Terms and Rules of Use of the Al-Mohammad Ali Family app are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws and regulations in force in the State of Kuwait, subject to mandatory legal provisions and the applicable agreements governing distribution of the app through the Apple App Store.", "The app administration seeks to resolve complaints and disputes arising from the use of its services amicably, by receiving and examining complaints and communicating with the parties concerned.", "Users may submit a complaint about the services, content, or decisions relating to their membership. The app administration will review and respond to the complaint within seven (7) calendar days from the date it is received.", "If an amicable settlement cannot be reached, either party may refer the matter to the competent courts of the State of Kuwait in accordance with the jurisdictional rules established by law, without any requirement to exhaust amicable settlement procedures and without prejudice to the rights of litigation established by law.", "Apple is not a party to these rules governing the family services provided by the app, and bears no obligation to manage the family tree, review content, or resolve disputes between members, without prejudice to any obligations or rights established under the applicable Apple agreements or relevant laws."], "summary": "These rules are governed by the laws of the State of Kuwait; we seek amicable settlement first."}, {"id": "contact", "title": "Contacting the App Administration", "lines": ["Users may contact the Al-Mohammad Ali Family app administration regarding enquiries, complaints, appeals, privacy requests, data correction, account deletion, and reports of violations via the official email address: info@almohali.com", "Contacting the administration by email is not a requirement for requesting account deletion, as a deletion request can be started directly from within the app in accordance with the Privacy Policy."], "summary": "For any question, appeal or request: info@almohali.com"}]}]}$j$::jsonb where key = 'legal_content_en';
